{"version":"1","id":"kantancoding","handle":"kantancoding","name":"Kantan Coding","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--FBdOHLfr--/f_auto/v1729363355/logos/kantancoding","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.7161,"y":-7.9564,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":60,"newest_post_at":"2026-04-27T14:00:06.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-10-28T07:47:41.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.008333,"listicle_ratio":0.083333,"question_ratio":0.016667,"avg_read_time":14.383333,"summary_length_avg":405.614035,"title_length_avg":43.816667,"title_length_var":169.649722,"tag_entropy":3.297497,"tag_diversity":0.683333,"top_tag_share":0.15,"avg_upvotes":1.55,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.1,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.074468,"zero_engagement_share":0.783333,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.757006,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.034483},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-1.7059,6.1029],"cadence_depth":[-3.2206,7.8971],"hype_variety":[0.5441,1.3088],"title_style":[0.0,9.1765]},"top_tags":[["golang",17],["general-programming",8],["microservices",6],["productivity",5],["webdev",5],["ai",5],["machine-learning",4],["python",4]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Linus's Laws of Writing Readable Code","speed up development with these command-line tools","Three laws of writing testable code"],"outlier":["golang context package explained: the package that changed concurrency forever"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"5Qt1yaj1o","title":"Nasa's Laws of Writing Readable Code","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=av0O_Lb8JbQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/nasa-s-laws-of-writing-readable-code-5qt1yaj1o","summary":"Drawing from NASA's coding standards, this covers three key principles for writing readable and maintainable code: keeping functions small and focused on a single responsibility to avoid excessive indirection, declaring data objects at the smallest possible scope to reduce side effects and race conditions, and enforcing access control (private/protected) rather than relying on comments to limit a method's exposed surface area.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/av0O_Lb8JbQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T14:00:06.000Z"},{"id":"cvKM81mwu","title":"Golang's 3 Concurrency Primitives - Pure Elegance","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6a0SIzmp91Q","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/golang-s-3-concurrency-primitives---pure-elegance-cvkm81mwu","summary":"An overview of Go's three core concurrency primitives: goroutines (using the `go` keyword), channels, and the select statement. Covers the fork-join concurrency model, how channels enable communication between goroutines, how WaitGroups synchronize completion, and how the select statement with a for-select loop handles multiple channels in long-lived programs.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/6a0SIzmp91Q/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-12T14:00:09.000Z"},{"id":"vhoNaYLjp","title":"Three laws of writing testable code","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bydOmLHyG_8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-3-laws-of-writing-testable-code-vhonayljp","summary":"Three fundamental principles for writing testable code: use dependency injection to decouple components, leverage interfaces to abstract external dependencies, and separate functions into single responsibilities. Demonstrates these concepts through a payment processing example, showing how to isolate code from external APIs like Stripe for effective unit testing.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bydOmLHyG_8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":16,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2025-07-28T17:05:44.000Z"},{"id":"6Cix0OXtj","title":"The 3 Laws of Writing Testable Code","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2U0YeskRMlY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-3-laws-of-writing-testable-code-6cix0oxtj","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2U0YeskRMlY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-07-28T14:30:41.000Z"},{"id":"5egEdNeGS","title":"speed up development with these command-line tools","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LIzM0aDRm6k","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/3-command-line-hacks-for-blazingly-fast-dev-linux-mac--5egednegs","summary":"Discover essential command-line hacks to boost productivity on Linux and Mac using tools like FZF and Tmux. Learn how FZF can simplify command histories and directory navigation, Tmux can streamline multi-container setups, and Zsh auto-suggestions can facilitate easier command recall.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LIzM0aDRm6k/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":24,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2025-05-03T14:00:35.000Z"},{"id":"ccAnVofE2","title":"Code Vulnerabilities: A Warning","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qHa0h8SWI00","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/code-vulnerabilities-a-warning-ccanvofe2","summary":"Writing code involves being cautious about security vulnerabilities. Common exploits include directory traversal, SQL injection, and cross-site scripting (XSS). These vulnerabilities often stem from naive trust in user input, highlighting the need for secure coding practices to safeguard against potential attacks.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/qHa0h8SWI00/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-05T15:24:38.000Z"},{"id":"RLijxLepq","title":"Common coding mistakes and how to avoid them","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bZPE4qd5-pI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/4-notorious-coding-mistakes-that-make-you-look-bad-rlijxlepq","summary":"The post identifies and explains four common coding mistakes often made by beginners, including using uninitialized variables, missing a semicolon in a for loop, using the assignment operator instead of the equality operator, and making off-by-one errors with array indices. These errors are broken down and ways to fix them are suggested to help improve coding practices.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bZPE4qd5-pI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-25T12:12:37.000Z"},{"id":"M5PcPBjwO","title":"The AI Deception Game","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YQBl7dW-gUw","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-ai-deception-game-m5pcpbjwo","summary":"The post argues that the portrayal of AI by billionaires and big tech CEOs is exaggerated and possibly deceptive. It explains that these players benefit from misleading the public about AI's capabilities, particularly with claims about achieving Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) soon. The author breaks down the differences between generative AI and AGI, emphasizing that the current state of generative AI, such as next token prediction models, is far from achieving true AGI. The narrative suggests that redefining AGI to fit closer timelines benefits companies and investors by driving hype and funding.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YQBl7dW-gUw/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-24T13:14:14.000Z"},{"id":"jIhbGTEXB","title":"Golang's Hidden Features","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lD8HBmVmwrM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/golang-s-hidden-features-jihbgtexb","summary":"Discover some of Golang's lesser-known features such as type conversions, implicit interface implementations, and the ability to assign methods to arbitrary types. Learn how these features can simplify your code and enhance functionality.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lD8HBmVmwrM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":8,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-12-23T08:56:31.000Z"},{"id":"JR81QTawu","title":"Abstraction Vs Code Readability","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=75vVcB2UPaQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/abstraction-vs-code-readability-jr81qtawu","summary":"Understanding how abstraction impacts code readability is crucial. While excessive abstraction can make code difficult to reason about, especially with few components, it is beneficial for managing complexity as the number of components grows. Properly encapsulating behaviors within classes can make the code more maintainable and reduce cognitive load for developers.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/75vVcB2UPaQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-26T13:00:07.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["cozmouz","veryacademy","welchlabsvideo","codebullet","noboilerplate"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"cozmouz","handle":"cozmouz","name":"cozmouz","is_squad":false,"x":-4.713,"y":-8.2442,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":18,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--lkC65Hg9--/f_auto/v1747295250/logos/cozmouz","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.35455,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":11.611111,"tag_diversity":0.555556},"top_tags_preview":[["machine-learning",18],["ai",16],["reinforcement-learning",11]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.5588,-0.9706],"cadence_depth":[-8.5,7.1912],"hype_variety":[-6.0294,-9.0147],"title_style":[-6.1029,-3.7206]}},{"id":"veryacademy","handle":"veryacademy","name":"Very Academy","is_squad":false,"x":-4.7805,"y":-8.2476,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":253,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s---JstyVnm--/f_auto/v1721572432/logos/veryacademy","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":5.227278,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":8.608696,"tag_diversity":0.118577},"top_tags_preview":[["django",148],["database",87],["postgresql",84]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-2.8088,-6.6176],"cadence_depth":[4.1176,5.0147],"hype_variety":[-6.6765,-4.75],"title_style":[-6.6765,-5.7059]}},{"id":"welchlabsvideo","handle":"welchlabsvideo","name":"Welch Labs","is_squad":false,"x":-5.02,"y":-8.2925,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":56,"image":"https